@page "/components/modalservice"
@page "/components/promodalservice"

<PageOutlet Url="components/modalservice"
            Title="ModalService"
            Description="BitModalService shows a BitModal with any content from anywhere in the app, and hands back a reference that closes it and completes with its answer." />

<DemoPage Name="ModalService"
          Description="BitModalService shows a BitModal with any content - a component, a Type or markup - from anywhere in the app: a service, a view model, a handler. Each Show hands back a BitModalReference that closes the modal, completes with its answer and says whether the user dismissed it. A BitModalParameters customizes the modal around the content with the same options as BitModal, plus a close guard and a navigation policy."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          GitHubUrl="Surfaces/Modal/BitModalService.cs"
          GitHubDemoUrl="Surfaces/Modal/BitModalServiceDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            Mount one <b>BitModalContainer</b> in the layout, in the same interactive render mode as the components
            that show modals - a modal shown with no container is not rendered, and the service logs it. Register the
            service <b>Scoped</b> on Blazor Server; a singleton is only safe on WebAssembly and Hybrid.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode"
                     CodeFiles="@example1CodeFiles" Id="example1">
            <div>
                <b>Show&lt;T&gt;</b> renders the component as the content; the content closes its own modal through the
                cascaded <b>BitModalReference</b>. <b>BitModalParameters</b> adds the chrome: <b>HeaderText</b> also
                names the dialog for screen readers - without it, give the modal an <b>AriaLabel</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowModal">Show</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="ShowChromeModal">With header &amp; footer</BitButton>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Markup as content" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                <b>Show</b> also takes a <b>RenderFragment</b>, for content not worth a component of its own. The
                reference's <b>Content</b> stays null, since markup is no component instance.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitButton OnClick="ShowMarkupModal">Show markup</BitButton>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Awaiting a result" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode"
                     CodeFiles="@example3CodeFiles" Id="example3">
            <div>
                <b>CloseWith</b> answers the modal, and <b>Result</b> / <b>GetResult&lt;T&gt;</b> complete with that
                answer. A dismissal answers null (the type's default), so <b>IsDismissed</b> tells "walked away" from
                "answered with nothing".
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitButton OnClick="ShowConfirmModal">Delete the project</BitButton>
            <div>Answer: [@confirmAnswer]</div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Reaching the content" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4">
            <div>
                The content is created when the container renders, after <b>Show</b> returns. <b>GetContentAsync&lt;T&gt;</b>
                waits for <b>Rendered</b> and hands the instance back. The <b>parameters factory</b> overload goes the
                other way: it receives the reference before the content is built, so a content parameter can use it -
                a callback that closes this very modal, or its id.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitButton OnClick="ShowContentReachingModal">Show and count</BitButton>
            <div>The content reported: [@contentReport]</div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Guarding the close" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode"
                     CodeFiles="@example5CodeFiles" Id="example5">
            <div>
                <b>CanClose</b> is asked before the user closes the modal (close button, overlay, Escape) and by
                <b>TryClose</b>; answering false keeps it open. <b>Close</b>, <b>CloseWith</b>, <b>CloseAll</b> and a
                close on navigation are the app's own and skip it. Type in the field, then try to close.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowGuardedModal">Rename the project</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="TryCloseGuardedModal">TryClose it from here</BitButton>
            </div>
            <div>Last attempt: [@guardReport]</div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Updating an open modal" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
            <div>
                <b>Update</b> replaces the parameters of an open modal and re-renders it. After mutating a parameters
                object in place, call <b>Refresh</b> instead.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitButton OnClick="ShowUpdatingModal">Show, then update it</BitButton>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Persistent modals" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode"
                     CodeFiles="@example7CodeFiles" Id="example7">
            <div>
                A <b>persistent</b> modal outlives its container: the service keeps it and hands it to the next
                container that mounts - even one mounting after the modal was shown. Any other modal closes, with a
                null result, when its container goes. Show one of each, then unmount the container.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowPersistentModal">Show a persistent modal</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="ShowOrdinaryModal">Show an ordinary one</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Text" OnClick="ToggleDemoContainer">
                    @(isDemoContainerMounted ? "Unmount the container" : "Mount the container again")
                </BitButton>
            </div>
            <div>Container: [@(isDemoContainerMounted ? "mounted" : "unmounted")]</div>
            <div>Persistent modal: [@DescribeModal(persistentModal)]</div>
            <div>Ordinary modal: [@DescribeModal(ordinaryModal)]</div>

            @if (isDemoContainerMounted)
            {
                <DemoModalContainer Service="demoModalService" />
            }
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Closing on navigation" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
            <div>
                Modals close when the path changes - a query string or fragment does not count.
                <b>CloseOnNavigation = false</b> keeps one open across routes (a sign-in prompt, a running upload);
                set it on the container's <b>ModalParameters</b> for all of them.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowNavigationModal">Show a modal</BitButton>
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowLingeringModal">Show one that stays</BitButton>
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="NavigateWithQuery">Change the query string (both stay)</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="NavigateToAnotherPage">Go to another page</BitButton>
            </div>
            <div>Modal: [@DescribeNavigationModal(navigationModal)]</div>
            <div>Modal that stays: [@DescribeNavigationModal(lingeringModal)]</div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Tracking open modals" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
            <div>
                <b>OpenModals</b> is a snapshot of the open modals, <b>GetModal</b> finds one by id and
                <b>CloseAll</b> closes them all (a sign-out). <b>OnAddModal</b> / <b>OnCloseModal</b> report every modal
                shown and closed, whoever showed it. <b>IsContainerAvailable</b> says whether a Show would render now.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowStackedModal">Show one more</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="CloseAllModals">Close all</BitButton>
            </div>
            <div>
                Open: [@modalService.OpenModals.Count] &nbsp; Shown: [@shownCount] &nbsp; Closed: [@closedCount]
                &nbsp; Container mounted: [@modalService.IsContainerAvailable]
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example10CsharpCode"
                     CodeFiles="@example10CodeFiles" Id="example10">
            <div>
                A <b>BitParams</b> around the container hands a <b>BitModalParams</b> to every modal it renders, and to
                every <b>BitModal</b> in markup below it. They are defaults: the container's <b>ModalParameters</b> and
                each showing's own parameters win over them.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowCascadedModal">Takes the cascade</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="ShowCascadedOwnModal">Its own position</BitButton>
            </div>

            <BitParams Parameters="modalParams">
                <DemoModalContainer Service="paramsModalService" />
            </BitParams>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style &amp; Class" RazorCode="@example11RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example11CsharpCode" Id="example11">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> and <b>Class</b> reach the root of the modal; <b>Styles</b> and <b>Classes</b> reach each
                part. The public <b>--bit-Modal-*</b> variables (see the <BitLink Href="/components/modal#css-variables-section">BitModal</BitLink>
                page) inherit, so a <b>Style</b> sets them for one modal, and the container's <b>ModalParameters</b>
                for all of them.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-box">
                <BitButton OnClick="ShowCssVariablesModal">CSS variables</BitButton>
                <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="ShowStyledPartsModal">Styles</BitButton>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example12RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example12CsharpCode" Id="example12">
            <div>
                <b>Dir = BitDir.Rtl</b> lays the modal out right-to-left, chrome included; <b>Start</b>/<b>End</b>
                positions follow along.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div dir="rtl">
                <BitButton Dir="BitDir.Rtl" OnClick="ShowRtlModal">باز کردن مُدال</BitButton>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
